---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SEO from "../components/SEO.astro";
const LAST_UPDATED = "2026-10-11";
const CONTACT_EMAIL = "ajmalsworkshop@gmail.com";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <SEO slot="head" title="Privacy Policy | Embedded & Circuits" description="How this site handles data, cookies, analytics, and advertising." path="/privacy/" />
  <div class="container">
    <header class="archive-head">
      <span class="kicker">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-container article-body" style="padding: 0; max-width: 44rem; padding-bottom: var(--space-12);">
    <p>
      This site is a personal blog. It has no accounts, no logins, and no
      user-submitted content. This policy explains what third-party services
      run when you visit, what they collect, and the choices and rights you have.
    </p>

    <h2>Services this site uses</h2>
    <p>
      This site is static and does not require an account to read. The following
      third-party services run when you visit:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics (GA4)</strong> — measures traffic and how the
        site is used, using cookies and similar identifiers. Google may process
        data such as pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser
        type, and a randomly generated identifier.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong> — serves the advertising on this site.
        Google and its partners may use cookies, web beacons, and IP addresses
        to serve ads, including personalised ads based on your prior visits to
        this and other websites.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts and delivers the site, and may log
        standard request data (IP address, user agent) for security and
        performance. See
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no tracking cookies of its own. It stores one small item in
      your browser's local storage to remember your cookie choice, which contains
      no personal data. The third parties above may set cookies or use similar
      technologies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics</strong> sets cookies to distinguish visitors
        and measure usage. IP addresses are anonymised. You can opt out with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on
        </a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, together with third-party vendors and
        ad networks, uses cookies to serve and measure ads. Google's use of
        advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you
        based on your visits to this and other sites. You can opt out of
        personalised advertising in your
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>,
        or opt out of many third-party vendor cookies at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> may process request logs to deliver the site
        and serve pages securely.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Google explains how it uses information from sites that use its services in
      <a href="https://www.google.com/policies/privacy/partners/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or apps
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your consent</h2>
    <p>
      On your first visit, a notice lets you accept all cookies or allow only
      those needed to run the site. Analytics and advertising storage stay
      disabled until you accept, implemented using Google Consent Mode. You can
      change your choice at any time by clearing this site's data in your
      browser; the notice will then appear again on your next visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      Whichever region you are in, you can control cookies through your browser
      settings and block trackers with browser extensions. In addition:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If you are in the EEA, the UK, or Switzerland, you have the right to
        access, correct, delete, and restrict processing of your personal data,
        and to object to personalised advertising.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you are a California resident, you have the right to know what
        personal information is collected and to opt out of its "sale" or
        "sharing" for cross-context behavioural advertising. This site does not
        sell personal information itself; you can exercise this right by
        rejecting non-essential cookies and using the opt-out links above.
      </li>
      <li>
        To make a request, email the address below. Because the site stores no
        personal data of its own, requests are passed to the relevant third party
        where applicable.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not store personal data itself. Retention of any data
      collected by the third-party services above is governed by their own
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly
      collect personal information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated from time to time. The "last updated" date at the
      top reflects the most recent change.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
